{"id": "EUVD-2026-107005", "enisaUuid": "2373e33c-fcd7-33db-9e24-c352a16f8d9e", "description": "vLLM before 0.31.0 contains a cache aliasing vulnerability that allows authenticated attackers to collide shared cache keys by supplying caller-controlled values such as EXIF ImageID or cache_salt. Attackers can set a UUID EXIF ImageID to receive another request's cached processed media, or match cache_salt to a LoRA name to reuse first-block KV state.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T00:36:30", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T00:36:30", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/security/advisories/GHSA-rh6f-3x46-j33q", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/vllm-before-0.31.0-cross-request-cache-aliasing-via-exif-imageid-and-prefix-cache-keys"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-114054", "GHSA-72rf-5fg2-rm98"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.28, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "89e75bb6-437c-37d9-af4c-389df836e46a", "product": {"name": "vllm", "vendor": {"name": "vllm-project"}}, "product_version": "0 <0.31.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "cff9f19e-e5e5-3cae-8e68-304d0c9fc5e9", "vendor": {"name": "vllm-project"}}], "isExploited": false}